# 5. Complete PostgreSQL database design

I recommend separating the database into functional groups. The following tables form the required foundation.

## A. User and account database

| Table               | Main columns                                   |
| ------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |
| `users`             | id, name, email, phone, password_hash, status  |
| `roles`             | id, role_name                                  |
| `user_roles`        | user_id, role_id                               |
| `user_addresses`    | id, user_id, address, city, state, pincode     |
| `user_sessions`     | id, user_id, refresh_token_hash, expires_at    |
| `otp_verifications` | id, user_id, destination, otp_hash, expires_at |
| `user_preferences`  | user_id, language, notification_preferences    |

Roles: `BUYER`, `SELLER`, `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN`, `SUPPORT`.

One user can have multiple roles, for example a buyer can also become a seller.

## B. Seller database

| Table                  | Main columns                                                |
| ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |
| `seller_profiles`      | id, user_id, business_name, seller_type, status             |
| `seller_documents`     | id, seller_id, document_type, file_url, verification_status |
| `seller_addresses`     | id, seller_id, address, city, state, pincode                |
| `seller_bank_accounts` | id, seller_id, encrypted_account, ifsc                      |
| `seller_stores`        | id, seller_id, slug, logo, banner, description              |
| `seller_policies`      | id, seller_id, return_policy, shipping_policy               |
| `seller_settings`      | seller_id, notification_settings, processing_time           |

## C. Product and inventory database

| Table                 | Main columns                                                    |
| --------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `categories`          | id, name, parent_id, slug                                       |
| `brands`              | id, name, logo                                                  |
| `products`            | id, seller_id, category_id, brand_id, name, description, status |
| `product_variants`    | id, product_id, sku, size, color, price, mrp                    |
| `product_images`      | id, product_id, image_url, sort_order                           |
| `product_videos`      | id, product_id, video_url, thumbnail_url                        |
| `product_attributes`  | id, product_id, attribute_name, attribute_value                 |
| `inventory`           | id, variant_id, available_qty, reserved_qty                     |
| `inventory_movements` | id, variant_id, movement_type, quantity, reference_id           |
| `product_reviews`     | id, product_id, buyer_id, rating, comment                       |

## D. Cart and order database

| Table                  | Main columns                                                      |
| ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `carts`                | id, buyer_id, status                                              |
| `cart_items`           | id, cart_id, variant_id, seller_id, quantity                      |
| `orders`               | id, order_number, buyer_id, total, status                         |
| `seller_orders`        | id, order_id, seller_id, subtotal, status                         |
| `order_items`          | id, seller_order_id, product_id, variant_id, quantity, unit_price |
| `order_addresses`      | id, order_id, address_type, address_snapshot                      |
| `order_status_history` | id, order_id, status, changed_at                                  |

Important: One customer order can contain products from multiple sellers. Each seller gets an independent suborder for packing, dispatch, delivery and returns.

## E. Payment and settlement database

| Table                    | Main columns                                          |
| ------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------- |
| `payments`               | id, order_id, gateway, transaction_id, amount, status |
| `payment_webhook_events` | id, gateway, event_id, payload, processed_at          |
| `commission_rules`       | id, category_id, commission_rate, fixed_fee           |
| `commission_entries`     | id, seller_order_id, gross_amount, commission_amount  |
| `seller_wallets`         | id, seller_id, available_balance, pending_balance     |
| `seller_ledger_entries`  | id, seller_id, entry_type, amount, reference_id       |
| `settlements`            | id, seller_id, amount, status, reference_number       |
| `settlement_items`       | id, settlement_id, ledger_entry_id                    |
| `refunds`                | id, payment_id, amount, reason, status                |

Use an auditable double-entry financial ledger for actual money movements. Wallet balances should be derived or reconciled against ledger entries, rather than trusted as the only financial record.

## F. Shipping database

| Table               | Main columns                                             |
| ------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |
| `shipping_partners` | id, name, integration_type, active                       |
| `shipping_rates`    | id, partner_id, origin, destination, rate                |
| `shipments`         | id, seller_order_id, partner_id, tracking_number, status |
| `shipment_items`    | id, shipment_id, order_item_id                           |
| `shipment_events`   | id, shipment_id, event, event_time                       |
| `pickup_requests`   | id, shipment_id, pickup_date, status                     |
| `shipping_labels`   | id, shipment_id, label_url                               |

## G. Coupons and loyalty database

| Table                  | Main columns                                                  |
| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `coupons`              | id, code, discount_type, discount_value, start_date, end_date |
