## C. Multi-seller checkout

Example:

A buyer orders:

- One shirt from Seller A.
- One pair of shoes from Seller B.
- One handbag from Seller C.

Prime Bazaar creates:

| Record            | Order      |
| ----------------- | ---------- |
| Customer order    | PB-10001   |
| Seller A suborder | PB-10001-A |
| Seller B suborder | PB-10001-B |
| Seller C suborder | PB-10001-C |

Each seller independently handles packing, shipping and returns. The buyer sees one combined order history with three shipment statuses.

## D. Live shopping workflow

1. Seller schedules a live session.
2. Admin reviews the session if required.
3. Seller starts broadcasting.
4. Buyers watch the live session.
5. Seller pins products on the video.
6. Buyers open product details.
7. Buyers add products to cart.
8. Orders are processed through normal checkout.

Live streaming should use a third-party video service initially rather than building your own streaming infrastructure.

